("v161", "type", "String")
("v161", "scalar", "✔ every embedded activity keeps its artwork visible independently of reader breakpoints (10.8288ms)\n✔ every encounter has a crawler-readable canonical page and complete sharing metadata (954.9156ms)\n✔ the social image is a real correctly described bitmap; sitemap includes all canonical pages (135.4184ms)\n✔ all local links and assets in the new static pages resolve within the publication (1502.012ms)\n✔ historical oracle bytes, passive resources and declared mechanism successors remain pinned (173.2137ms)\n✔ algebra owns the publication with the existing admission rules, ports and budget (38.3562ms)\n✔ reading paths connect the guided journey to research while microsites keep their own entrances (22.8631ms)\n✔ the homepage presents the hierarchy and preserves existing project entrances (2.2244ms)\n✔ Claimipedia has its own three-lens identity with accessible sections, local assets and quiet motion (10.1915ms)\n✔ purpose-first sharing cards have real raster bytes and consistent server-visible metadata (34.4424ms)\n✔ a fresh algebra build reproduces every publication artifact (85167.8181ms)\n✔ algebra remembers actual destination visits, deduplicates them and restores the map (31.0906ms)\n✔ reset clears only the atlas key and all seen labels (17.494ms)\n✔ untrusted saved text is bounded and restricted to known places (16.8551ms)\n✔ blocked storage stays nonfatal and reports the limit honestly (14.5653ms)\n✔ previews are dismissible and every pin has an ordinary link and readable label (7.988ms)\n✔ mobile taps preview a place before exploration, with no false seen mark (17.3514ms)\n✔ a destination restored from browser history marks itself again after a reset (1.3529ms)\n✔ the independent illustrated atlas preserves all forty destinations and return paths (46.445ms)\n✔ source ownership switches only after ordered module and lowering correspondence, then validation (11.5031ms)\n✔ stale, ambiguous, undeclared and non-corresponding migrations cannot stage (20.9983ms)\n✔ all six retained predecessors pass the actual authoring algebra, shared frontend and whole-module lowerer (17657.9314ms)\n✔ acceptance matches command identity, count, exit status and error rather than PASS strings or ok flags (12.1779ms)\n✔ retirement preserves exact helper bytes before deletion and ignores logs/directories (1.1791ms)\n✔ archive collisions refuse retirement and source switching before validation (2.1293ms)\n✔ clean verification requires a clean revision and absent build, installed dependencies and generated output (0.9897ms)\n✔ normal verification has no .build input and does not rewrite presentation evidence (213.2094ms)\n✔ snapshot comparison hashes binary input bytes and distinguishes an absent creation target (24.892ms)\n✔ retired helpers remain hashed evidence with no active executable counterpart (13.6253ms)\n✔ the authoring policy admits with only its declared generic mechanisms (278.5118ms)\n✔ previews validate without committing; apply commits the validated proposal before its receipt (4.2182ms)\n✔ bad authority, stale and repeated edits, no-ops and malformed proposals refuse before staging (6.8571ms)\n✔ failed publication validation cannot reach the commit effect (0.9651ms)\n✔ all build source owners remain editable; generator predecessors are inert and byte-identical (17.1206ms)\n✔ encounter: exact ordered JSON, whole lowered module and all original-coordinate statements (16337.3409ms)\n✔ source: exact ordered JSON, whole lowered module and all original-coordinate statements (222.5326ms)\n✔ microsite-ui: exact ordered JSON, whole lowered module and all original-coordinate statements (231.2658ms)\n✔ microsite-values: exact ordered JSON, whole lowered module and all original-coordinate statements (217.9505ms)\n✔ microsite-sourcery: exact ordered JSON, whole lowered module and all original-coordinate statements (168.6339ms)\n✔ microsite-temple-ui: exact ordered JSON, whole lowered module and all original-coordinate statements (781.9611ms)\n✔ all six explicit effect profiles link against the same supplied application closure (50.217ms)\n✔ each is profile-gated and preserves binding, ordered effects and non-accumulating scope (888.1213ms)\n✔ module-specific profiles refuse foreign source profiles, effects and undeclared callees (1392.7801ms)\n✔ JSON and candidate UI legs preserve ordered DOM/state effects, recipe values and crypto refusal (1075.8262ms)\n✔ the pre-switch JSON owner or post-switch Encounter owner is explicit, never a fallback (5623.3269ms)\n✔ all 48 bounded reviews correspond to the original Claimipedia evaluator (84.7781ms)\n✔ reasoning exposes failed conditions, omitted evidence and the equal-weight blind spot (7.9051ms)\n✔ real Worldwright Markdown projects headings, two tables, strong text and honest source-relative links (112.0053ms)\n✔ Markdown projection preserves fenced blank lines, lists, quotes and literal unsafe markup (78.9433ms)\n✔ shared Markdown lexer preserves every source code unit and gives syntax real roles (138.0049ms)\n✔ readable expression layout breaks long groups without modifying its input model (2.9061ms)\n✔ Markdown projection refuses documents outside its declared bounds (34.584ms)\n✔ every source query has a readable definition and exact structural statement coordinates (525.5006ms)\n✔ readable module inspection refuses missing queries and does not execute source effects (1.4666ms)\n✔ the module selector projects the bound query through the shared presenter using read-only DOM effects (1132.2972ms)\n✔ the standalone module page replaces the raw-JSON entrance and states the authoring boundary (42.8035ms)\n✔ microsite and every declared event root admit against the existing kernel and grants (1711.0981ms)\n✔ the live title edit uses the original patch contract and updates exactly its source-derived views (1743.8164ms)\n✔ wrong value types and fields without a declared inverse route refuse (770.4685ms)\n✔ every inspector selection exposes the current exact text and a shared highlighted projection (2513.6455ms)\n✔ boot, edit, inspection and reset share one session and preserve the accepted candidate on refusal (3330.7717ms)\n✔ the source owners reuse the retained compiler and leave the original microsites intact (9.4183ms)\n✔ each of the ten identified areas has a distinct, sourced and rendered entrance and continuation (7.3753ms)\n✔ every selected corpus source preserves its retained capture and recorded hash (42.1901ms)\n✔ optional readings have explicit scope and do not gate a scientific route (0.7508ms)\n✔ the finite compatibility example exposes its exact allowed set (0.5172ms)\n✔ the pattern counter applies the declared integer action without treating ornament as evidence (0.3989ms)\n✔ positive-response admission agrees with the smallest eigenvalue on every displayed matrix (3.8317ms)\n✔ the repetition-code claim holds over both original bits and all eight received words (0.444ms)\n✔ the numerical memory illustration remains finite and changes when coupling is removed (0.3763ms)\n✔ block aggregation preserves total while discarding within-block arrangements (0.4254ms)\n✔ the ranking desk discloses a reversible arithmetic preference rather than changing the options (0.4645ms)\n✔ reported rate cards retain the source decimals and their model-local intermediate optimum (0.7434ms)\n✔ encounters and paths beyond a territory preserve real destinations and source identity (2.1512ms)\n✔ the illustrative measuring axis resolves a vertical unit difference only as it rotates toward it (1.7238ms)\n✔ lifting the map preserves the record while exposing conditions and limits separately (1.4716ms)\n✔ territories locate each scene exactly once and reflective studies retain their declared material (0.5912ms)\n✔ all passages resolve, all scenes are reachable, and every scene has a route back (22.84ms)\n✔ each scene retains source identity and every cited corpus capture exists locally (9.9574ms)\n✔ personal passages are marked as personal and cannot be mistaken for model results (0.5803ms)\n✔ the homepage hierarchy preserves the author order and routes every tool to its own microsite (29.4384ms)\n✔ source snapshots preserve their hashes and exact upstream lines when the recorded source is available (173.719ms)\n✔ all published capability edges are extracted by the existing REL parser with exact source bindings (224.9103ms)\n✔ sharing uses exact typed identity and counts each consumer once (4.8312ms)\n✔ malformed, unsupported and stale source-line bindings refuse rather than fabricating connections (4.9735ms)\n✔ source inspection exposes receipts, consumers and honest missing edges with the existing source presenter (5.5157ms)\n✔ the admitted viewer highlights source and its actual sharing definition with separate exact hash bases (2381.128ms)\n✔ the opening fold has three illustrated entrances and moves questions and applications to their own destinations (1.9057ms)\n✔ Mission Control is a first-class Sourcery tool, linked from Science, with inspected sources and native workflow disclosure (1.2699ms)\n✔ purpose types distinguish all cards while Creator Studio completes six developing entries (9.0739ms)\n✔ SHA-256 fallback agrees with Web Crypto for Unicode and padding boundaries (18.7352ms)\n✔ Temple Merkle drawing geometry, order, labels and fresh highlights match original SVG effects (271.1126ms)\n✔ Temple explanatory lessons match every preset, identity and refusal branch in the source (429.9698ms)\n✔ Sourcery flood scatter, waves and broom poses match original motion at sampled frames (181.6866ms)\n✔ Temple sky scatter, twinkle, parallax, motes and respawn match original canvas effects (225.8125ms)\n✔ Temple constellation geometry, glow, sparks and rings match original canvas effects (79.5206ms)\n✔ reduced motion and hidden documents draw still frames without scheduling animation (9.2528ms)\n✔ film seeking preserves range endpoints and the metadata/blob fallback sequence (3.736ms)\n✔ Temple genesis identities, canonical bytes, state roots and Merkle levels match the original (79.3878ms)\n✔ every preset, identity and false-root choice reproduces the original proposal, verdict and witness (3061.5019ms)\n✔ amendment, refusals, stale basis, replay and both forgeries preserve the exact history boundary (897.7364ms)\n✔ Sourcery intent classification and all proposal templates match the original source (979.9009ms)\n✔ Sourcery sealing, returns, witness verification, tampering and restoration match the original (68.8715ms)\n✔ microsite-lamp: ordered surface, complete lowering and original-coordinate coverage agree (14233.7284ms)\n✔ microsite-motion: ordered surface, complete lowering and original-coordinate coverage agree (420.5849ms)\n✔ microsite-temple-motion: ordered surface, complete lowering and original-coordinate coverage agree (634.4665ms)\n✔ microsite-media: ordered surface, complete lowering and original-coordinate coverage agree (184.9692ms)\n✔ batch frontends link against the supplied main closure and refuse foreign profiles and effects (3241.492ms)\n✔ empty catch bodies are profile-gated; empty try bodies and malformed indentation still refuse (821.7548ms)\n✔ ownership is singular and every selected readable module has a source-bound Inspect page (697.9549ms)\n✔ Inspect uses exact authored slices and refuses stale or undeclared source bindings without executing them (2631.9998ms)\n✔ all four recomposed documents retain their independently compared source structure and reading (41.8688ms)\n✔ microsite navigation and referenced resources stay inside the ecosystem and resolve, including fragments (72.1261ms)\n✔ every captured microsite asset and both complete stylesheets retain their exact bytes (97.6818ms)\n✔ original application JavaScript is an oracle only; shipping behaviour is algebra-owned (8.7985ms)\n✔ every project microsite has exactly one algebra-owned return to the main catalogue (25.9727ms)\n✔ whole-module source compiles to exact ordered JSON with no profile or implicit entrypoint (5583.2337ms)\n✔ every actual statement has an original-coordinate source origin (16.4376ms)\n✔ the entire lowered module is identical through the existing lowerer (1360.857ms)\n✔ JSON and readable-source legs agree on real documents, formatting, faults and ordered effects (3290.9817ms)\n✔ the successor changes only the declared lexer separator and safe record-key formatting (4.4415ms)\n✔ malformed control syntax, unsafe names, unknown operators and mismatched profile refuse (136.7533ms)\n✔ compiler identity refuses changed dependencies before compilation (3.4513ms)\n✔ linking traverses folds and error handlers and refuses undeclared calls or effects (47.2669ms)\n✔ a readable source edit changes execution through the existing lowerer and kernel (59.1446ms)\n✔ the authority switch selects Encounter exclusively and binds generated JSON to its source hash (4.1247ms)\n✔ Inspect displays exact authored characters using compiler ranges rather than regenerated notation (1295.5928ms)\n✔ all bundled research sources preserve their recorded bytes (105.7048ms)\n✔ static entry points and module imports remain relative to their publication path (399.864ms)\n✔ migrated finite models reproduce every slider setting and bit pattern (41.2563ms)\n✔ both numerical memory trajectories and all plotted coordinates retain exact predecessor results (97.876ms)\n✔ algebra-owned workshop sessions reproduce source edits, overlays, generated HTML and refusal boundaries (6088.2058ms)\n✔ forty activity source documents retain controls and contain no executable source (0.529ms)\n✔ the published execution graph contains only admitted bundles and generic native mechanisms (210.2955ms)\n✔ whole-bundle auditing rejects extra executable code and altered native mechanisms (9.3463ms)\n✔ document observation executes supplied transformation plans without reader defaults (0.8224ms)\n✔ frame capability choice comes from algebra within the native script-free ceiling (3.1292ms)\n✔ every stop has an authored reading and every offered term has a definition (2.7822ms)\n✔ all sources have a plain introduction while original research and full source notes remain available (59.8797ms)\n✔ rate cards explain the same reported values as rounded percentages (1.3547ms)\n✔ the historical workshop oracle preserves its exact kernel and native function bodies (7.3861ms)\n✔ workshop is a connected tour stop with real static resources (0.9988ms)\n✔ all unaffected scenes retain the captured content of the other changes (2.3741ms)\n▶ portable engine preserves source/overlay ownership and unchanged-state refusals\n  ✔ starts from the checked fixture (0.3807ms)\n  ✔ source edit updates page and row, preserving overlay (0.4096ms)\n  ✔ overlay edits its literal and escapes generated markup (0.3844ms)\n  ✔ refuse /EC-T007/ (800.6652ms)\n  ✔ refuse /EC-E010/ (68.0245ms)\n  ✔ refuse /LAB-E001/ (0.3584ms)\n  ✔ stale basis refuses (0.3886ms)\n  ✔ original fixture is unchanged (0.7698ms)\n  ✔ new session starts independently (1010.7271ms)\n✔ portable engine preserves source/overlay ownership and unchanged-state refusals (5491.495ms)\n✔ portable execution agrees with direct native fixture execution for the same edits (7150.0421ms)\nℹ tests 154\nℹ suites 0\nℹ pass 154\nℹ fail 0\nℹ cancelled 0\nℹ skipped 0\nℹ todo 0\nℹ duration_ms 88238.447\n")
